  "security_implications": "The register drives rdata_q to all-ones on error_i, err_internal, or wr_req during a_ack. If downstream logic does not interpret all-ones as an error indication, a security-sensitive operation could proceed with invalid data. Specifically, when wr_req is true but error_i/err_internal are false, error_q remains 0 while rdata_q becomes all-ones, potentially allowing a write error to be misconstrued as a successful read with all-ones data. This could leak a constant or mask a real integrity error.",
